Notably, the proposed novel bi-phase system is different from reported interfacial growth wherein the MOF crystal growth is mainly happened at immiscible interface [12b, 13]. In order to investigate the crystal growth characteristics at different interface depth region (or concentration of the solution), we have selectively deposited MnBDC sheets onto $\mathsf{S i}/\mathsf{S i O}_{2}$ substrates which was held perpendicularly in the growth vial as shown in Figure 4a. This arrangement allowed us to collect synthesized MnBDC specimens in different segments of the interface region. Optical images in Figure 4c were taken at the marked positions including upper, intermediate and bottom areas indicated in schematic substrate.
